From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:11:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 104/111] Auto-scroll keeps the selection following and stops
 wasting frames

The selection stayed where the pointer left the preview while it
scrolled: the text runs at the edge kept being outranked by their own
last report at the same pointer position, and once the pointer was out
of the window it was not known at all. Each scroll step now lets them
compare afresh at the pointer's last known place.

The preview also scrolls when the pointer is within 24 px of its top or
bottom, so a maximised window works. It scrolls on a 60 Hz timer that
runs only while a selection is dragged at an edge, not by requesting a
frame from every frame, and stops at the top or bottom of the document.
A drag ends when the button goes up anywhere or the window loses focus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

